On 13/06/17 22:51, Selva Nair wrote:
> It takes only a few line sof code to exploit this on XP -- I have not
> been able to exploit this on Vista but not 100% sure it has been
> fixed for good on Vista+.

But do we really care much for anything older than Win7 these days?  For
v2.3, perhaps yes - but v2.4 is the one introducing the interactive service.

WindowsXP (and Vista) are old, even unsupported by Microsoft (well,
mostly - they added a highly critical IE fix this week, but generally it
is dead).  So my opinion is that anything related to OpenVPN v2.4 and
newer on Windows versions older than Win7 can just burn and we'll
happily just observe it.

But at some point we will need to pull the WinXP/Vista support plug for
v2.3 and older too.  Like we did with Win2K a long time ago too.


